---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import siteConfig from '@/site-config'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CV - Shad Mirza"
  description="Professional CV of Shad Mirza - Senior Software Engineer at DigitalOcean GenAI"
>
  <article class="prose max-w-4xl">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Shad Mirza</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">Senior Software Engineer</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 mb-4">
        DigitalOcean GenAI • AI platforms, observability, agent systems
      </p>

      <!-- Contact Information -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6 text-sm">
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`} class="flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-blue-600">
          <i class="i-ri-mail-line"></i>
          {siteConfig.email}
        </a>
        <a href="tel:+91-9721442124" class="flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-blue-600">
          <i class="i-ri-phone-line"></i>
          +91-9721442124
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza" target="_blank" class="flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-blue-600">
          <i class="i-ri-github-line"></i>
          github.com/iamshadmirza
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/iamshadmirza/"
          target="_blank"
          class="flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-blue-600"
        >
          <i class="i-ri-linkedin-line"></i>
          linkedin.com/in/iamshadmirza
        </a>
        <a href="https://x.com/iamshadmirza" target="_blank" class="flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-blue-600">
          <i class="i-ri-twitter-x-line"></i>
          x.com/iamshadmirza
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 pb-2 !mt-0 !mb-4">Summary</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Senior Software Engineer at DigitalOcean GenAI (Nov 2025 – Present) with ~8 years across AI platforms,
        observability, and high-scale product. Currently on agent feedback and evaluation systems; previously AI
        Platform: day-0 model launches, Unified Batch Inference, and OpenTelemetry/customer metrics from scratch. Before
        that, platform and mobile at Hashnode (130M+ monthly API requests, 160K+ MAUs). Strong focus on ownership,
        reusable tooling, and cross-team delivery.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Skills -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 pb-2 !mt-0 !mb-6">
        Core Skills
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 !mt-0 !mb-3">Frontend Development</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>React.js & React Native</li>
            <li>TypeScript & JavaScript</li>
            <li>Next.js</li>
            <li>Redux, MobX, Context API</li>
            <li>TailwindCSS, Styled Components</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 !mt-0 !mb-3">Backend & APIs</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Node.js & Express.js</li>
            <li>Go</li>
            <li>GraphQL & REST APIs</li>
            <li>Inference / batch job APIs</li>
            <li>MongoDB, Redis, PostgreSQL</li>
            <li>Serverless & microservices</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 !mt-0 !mb-3">Cloud & Infrastructure</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Kubernetes / DOKS</li>
            <li>OpenTelemetry & customer metrics/logs</li>
            <li>AWS (Lambda, API Gateway, Step Functions)</li>
            <li>AWS (EventBridge, S3, EC2, SQS, SNS)</li>
            <li>Infrastructure as Code (SST, AWS CDK)</li>
            <li>CI/CD Pipelines</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 !mt-0 !mb-3">AI, Agents & Quality</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>GenAI platform APIs & model launches</li>
            <li>Agent feedback / evaluation loops</li>
            <li>Cursor skills & agent DX</li>
            <li>Jest & React Testing Library</li>
            <li>Cypress & Playwright</li>
            <li>TDD practices</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Experience -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 pb-2 !mt-0 !mb-6">
        Professional Experience
      </h2>

      <!-- DigitalOcean Experience -->
      <div class="mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold !mt-0 !mb-0">DigitalOcean (Remote)</h3>
          <span class="text-base text-gray-500">Nov 2025 – Present</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-4 !mt-0 !mb-4">Senior Software Engineer • GenAI</p>

        <div class="mb-4">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Agent feedback & evaluation (current)</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Building systems for agent feedback and evaluation: quality signals, tooling, and services that help teams
              measure and improve agent behavior.
            </li>
            <li>
              Carrying observability learnings into new work: treat telemetry and failure handling as first-class
              requirements, design for load/backpressure early, and lock auth/access paths before re-platforming.
            </li>
            <li>
              Introduced documentation-first discovery so teams align on written findings before implementation
              diverges.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-4">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">AI Platform</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Shipped day-one API integrations for major Claude and OpenAI model launches within hours of public
              announcement, matching top-tier cloud providers on time-to-market.
            </li>
            <li>
              Architected and led Unified Batch Inference; built the API server, ran the data migration, integrated the
              LiteLLM inference proxy, and added JWT auth in a single day to rescue an at-risk launch. Authored the
              official
              <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/introducing-batch-inference" target="_blank"
                >DigitalOcean launch post</a
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              Rewrote a third-party AI integration for security review, added concurrency rate limiting, and migrated
              from polling to webhooks for real-time customer status updates.
            </li>
            <li>
              Established GenAI observability from scratch: OpenTelemetry collectors across Kubernetes/DOKS clusters
              with no prior docs; migrated the org off scattered personal logging and helped sunset a legacy control
              plane that was a single point of failure.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built customer-facing metrics/logs paths from the ground up (foundational RFC); resolved 7+ PR cycles of
              blockers (protocol mismatches, broken log routing, collector OOMs). Tuned batch sizes from 10,000 to 1,000
              with custom memory limiters and retries.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built Cursor skills and playbooks that turned multi-hour OTel/metrics setup into self-serve work for other
              teams; used the same tooling to fix misaligned collector configs across 11 clusters in a day. Wrote Batch
              Inference OnCall debugging runbooks.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hashnode Experience -->
      <div class="mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold !mt-0 !mb-0">Hashnode (Remote)</h3>
          <span class="text-base text-gray-500">Feb 2020 – Nov 2025</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-4 !mt-0 !mb-4">
          Platform & Mobile • Bengaluru, Karnataka
        </p>

        <!-- Platform Engineer -->
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Platform Engineer</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Contributed to AWS serverless infrastructure supporting 160K+ MAU as part of the platform team.</li>
            <li>
              Built and led implementation of GitHub sync via webhooks and AWS Lambda which enabled documentations to be
              sourced from GitHub repository publishing 1k+ pages on every commit.
            </li>
            <li>
              Led development of an AI documentation assistant using OpenAI, LangChain, and Pinecone. Enabled natural
              language Q&A, summarization, and semantic search across technical content.
            </li>
            <li>
              Designed and contributed to key platform features including newsletter import, documentation export, spam
              filtering, and notification delivery.
            </li>
            <li>
              Played a key role in migrating the REST APIs to Serverless GraphQL Infra (SST & Apollo on AWS Lambda)
              serving 130M+ requests per month.
            </li>
            <li>
              Drove documentation strategy for Public GraphQL APIs, implemented SpectaQL-based tooling to streamline
              updates and improve developer experience.
            </li>
            <li>Created CI/CD pipelines to streamline development and improve DX.</li>
            <li>Set up unit testing for GraphQL and AWS infrastructure using Jest, boosting code reliability.</li>
            <li>Led mentoring and onboarding of 5+ engineers to ensure swift and effective team integration.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Mobile App Lead -->
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Mobile App Lead</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Led the development and shipped Hashnode's React Native app from scratch (50K MAUs), supporting
              deep-linked auth flows.
            </li>
            <li>
              Implemented CI/CD pipelines, analytics, versioning, and complex UX animations (36% rating improvement).
            </li>
            <li>Established TDD workflows reducing crash reports by 60%.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Full Stack Developer -->
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Full Stack Developer</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Contributed significantly to the major overhaul of Hashnode, migrating legacy code resulting in improved
              site performance, reduced technical debt, and optimized development efficiency.
            </li>
            <li>
              Led the development of a co-author feature allowing users to add multiple contributors to their articles.
            </li>
            <li>Delivered major features like newsletter import/export, analytics dashboard, and community widgets.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sheevoot Experience -->
      <div class="mb-6">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold !mt-0 !mb-0">Sheevoot Int Pvt. Ltd.</h3>
          <span class="text-base text-gray-500">Oct 2018 – Feb 2020</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-4 !mt-0 !mb-4">Bengaluru, Karnataka</p>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Mobile Application Engineer</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Led end-to-end design and development of the Easebuoy app, a pilot project deployed in Bengaluru and
              Indore, contributing to overall product launch success.
            </li>
            <li>
              Developed core app features including ride booking, food delivery, pickup-drop services, and car wash
              bookings, enhancing user convenience and engagement.
            </li>
            <li>Used React Native frontend and PHP/MySQL backend stack; supported 10K+ MAUs.</li>
            <li>
              Built multiple vendor-facing apps for operations (order management, logistics, delivery tracking, ride
              management).
            </li>
            <li>
              Integrated Google Maps/Directions APIs and conducted A/B testing with 100+ drivers and 200+ vendors.
            </li>
            <li>
              Collaborated with cross-functional stakeholders on roadmap planning, release cycles, app design, feature
              enhancements, and marketing strategies, ensuring alignment with business goals.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Other Notable Contributions -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 pb-2 !mt-0 !mb-6">
        Other Notable Contributions
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <li>
          Built
          <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza/to-onepager" target="_blank">to-onepager</a>, a Cursor skill that
          turns research and decision chats into short, grounded one-pagers and publishes them where teams already read.
        </li>
        <li>
          Built a cross-platform reusable component library and design system for React Native (
          <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza/react-native-design-system" target="_blank">RNDS</a>).
        </li>
        <li>Published author on DigitalOcean, Hashnode Engineering, LogRocket, Soshace, and Alligator.io.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Education -->
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 pb-2 !mt-0 !mb-6">Education</h2>
      <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-2">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold !mt-0 !mb-0">Dr APJ Abdul Kalam Technical University</h3>
        <span class="text-base text-gray-500">April 2014 - May 2018</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-2 !mt-0 !mb-2">Lucknow, U.P.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        B.Tech (Computer Science) – Top 3 academic rank in a cohort of 80+ students.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Download Section -->
    <section class="text-center mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600">
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">Download this CV as PDF</p>
      <a
        href="/ShadMirza-FullStackEngineer.pdf"
        download
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-medium transition-colors"
      >
        <i class="i-ri-download-line"></i>
        Download CV (PDF)
      </a>
    </section>
  </article></BaseLayout
>
